{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793714801,"nonce":"18dObxCSpS87kB3v7J6iPYDnqck=","message":"Implemented the fresh-constructor receiver path in 142b19055560926120418de961de3f24cd334c9d.\n\nThe typer retains receiver provenance for every tracked setmetatable write. Lowering proves straight-line fresh constructor bodies and single-assignment, uncaptured locals using its existing field-presence checks. That keeps a possibly absent NthToggle.new from being mistaken for a guaranteed own constructor. Every other write to the receiver's shape must be a birth or a different proven fresh local. Escapes, unknown metatables/code, debug rebinding, aliases, parameters, captured or reassigned locals, and unproved constructor bodies retain general dispatch. Constructor field writes with a possible __newindex handler are rejected as freshness proofs. The shape's layout, global class set and conservative inferred signatures stay unchanged. Facts are cleared between lowering passes, and receiver precision stops at a field access or call result.\n\nValidation:\n- Analysis-only stage: all 46 conformance categories and the first two proof tests passed before dispatch was changed.\n- Final: 107 test functions passed with cargo test --offline -j 2 -p zyntax_lua --release --features llvm-backend -- --test-threads=2, including both official Lua configurations, the whole-suite tests, memory pressure and typed paths. Existing KNOWN_FAILURES unchanged.\n- 21 new programs pinned against Lua 5.4.9 cover exact receivers, the listed rebinding routes, absent/replaced constructors, constructor publication, conditional/loop rebinding, shadowed builtins, __call/__index/__newindex, chained receivers and own methods. A structural test checks that each exact call contains only its own method target.\n- Clippy all-targets with warnings denied and formatting checked. Source changes are confined to zyntax_lua; no shared compiler or TypeScript code changed.\n\nThe actual method_call.lua chunk shrinks from 2338 instructions / 766 blocks / 199 calls to 1438 / 406 / 159 before optimization. Both receiver locals get the correct exact class. All lowered function dumps are byte-identical for binary_trees, closure_call, free_function_call, inlined_call, lambda_call, nbody, op_overload and records.\n\nNUC measurements: i5-1250P, taskset 0,2,4,6, release binaries built at parent 6a51e7a9ac821d21f6edab1bb5f2b51ed0358c2e, with only these three Lua source changes in the candidate. Both built with llvm-backend and report llvm with ZYLUA_LLVM=1. No cargo/rustc jobs during or between samples. Baseline/candidate/LuaJIT order alternated each round, output checked against Lua 5.4.\n- First 15 method_call samples: wall 52.588 -\u003e 41.063 ms; elapsed 9.320 -\u003e 7.571 ms. LuaJIT wall 6.209 / elapsed 4.301 ms.\n- Repeat, 21 samples: wall 51.749 -\u003e 40.455 ms (21.8% less); elapsed 9.370 -\u003e 7.454 ms (20.4% less). LuaJIT wall 6.186 / elapsed 4.290 ms.\n- All other 16 kernels ran five interleaved rounds with matching outputs. A closure_call outlier was checked over 21 more samples: wall 15.089 -\u003e 15.227 ms, overlapping ranges; its lowered HIR is byte-identical. No broad speedup is claimed.\n- Baseline binary SHA256 acc39739c073e62b0ee120c09431549aaab065c41a59bd7d0b526b57f3094215; candidate e2f95c1e8b9d4840b331da8028a7c7cc2f457cf582257a23cacb84d933c94a98.\n\nThe handoff's 27 ms / 1.6 ms estimate came from removing NthToggle, which changes the workload, and its mc_ctor.lua now uses separate constructors. Neither is an equivalent before/after control for the real benchmark. This change still loses to LuaJIT; remaining startup, callee preparation and guard costs remain under e8fe1d3. NthToggle.activate itself is unchanged at 305 lowered instructions / 97 blocks, including optional-field and error paths. A candidate trace still compiles lua$chunk in 18.15 ms, 14.46 ms in body preparation.\n\nThe NUC's pre-existing dirty checkout was stashed, restored and compared byte-for-byte afterward. Temporary binaries and scratch were removed. Raw local reports/logs are in /private/tmp/zyntax-exact-receivers/.","files":null}]}